## Choose your test

| What you want to check | Example | Tool |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A function or rule | Reject an order with quantity zero. | React Native Jest, Android JUnit, or iOS XCTest. |
| A component or state change | Show a sign-in error or update the Redux Toolkit order state. | The project's component and state test setup. |
| A journey in the installed app | Enter credentials, tap Sign in, and verify the next screen. | React Native WebdriverIO and Appium, Android Espresso, or iOS XCUITest. |

For the React Native device path, **WebdriverIO runs the test**, **Appium performs the taps and typing**, and **Sauce Labs provides the phone**. For native suites, Espresso or XCUITest performs the screen interactions through its configured device runner.

Start with the local tests for the feature you changed. Add the device journey required by your team's test strategy. A device test can cover several screens in one journey.

