## 9. Investigate a failed step

| Symptom | Inspect |
| --- | --- |
| Push starts no build. | GitLab webhook URL and test event, then the provisioning result. |
| Clone fails with `Permission denied (publickey)`. | Bitrise SSH public key and the GitLab deploy key. |
| Internal step cannot be fetched. | Bitrise read access to the referenced step repository. |
| Provisioning returns 401, 403, or 404. | Token validity, scope, project path, and role. |
| Provisioning rejects the local env file. | Git ignore rules and valid Bash quoting. |
| Framework package cannot be resolved. | Actual release tag, registry/repository access, and installed dependencies. |
| App shows the Metro error screen. | Uploaded variant and bundled JavaScript in the Release test artifact. |
| Native module is missing. | Linking and compatibility with the app's React Native architecture. |
| Test account is rejected. | Matching fixture/backend account and build/test credential values. |
| Element is missing. | Accessibility IDs, keyboard state, foreground app, and BasePage diagnostics. |
| Sauce authentication returns 401. | Account region and protected credential bindings. |
| No device is available. | Device pattern and account capacity. |
| Teams posts no card. | Workflows URL, enabled flow, expected JSON schema, and workflow run history. |
| Security check finds generated or tracked secrets. | Rotate exposed values, remove tracked secret files, and restore the empty build-config placeholder. |

